  "final_message": "I haven't removed anything yet, because the premise doesn't hold. `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` on `OrderPlaced`, and it requires it.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34`** calls `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. A missing `channel` makes it throw `ContractViolationError`, and the whole event is rejected.\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17`** writes `channel` into the `orders` table, which is described in its README.\n- **`analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88`** has a test named \"requires channel\".\n\nIf we drop `channel` from the event, `analytics-ingest` would reject every `OrderPlaced` message. No analytics rows would be written for new orders. That repo is another team's, and it's read-only for us.\n\n`billing-service` only uses `channel` in its test helpers, and its test at `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined`. It looks safe.\n\nIn this repo, `channel` is used in these places:\n- `src/core/order.ts` (model, validation, `CHANNELS`)\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- the tests\n- the README and CLAUDE.md examples\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n1. **Remove it from the model and the event, as you asked.** The analytics team would have to make `channel` optional or drop it first. I'd treat that as a prerequisite.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and the API only.** The event would keep `channel`. That isn't really possible without a value to fill it, so it would mean a default or a deprecation period.\n3. **Wait** until `analytics-ingest` has changed.\n\nTell me which and I'll make the change. For option 1 I'll also update the tests and docs, then run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run arch`.",
